    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im having some trouble with these walnut dovetails i'm cutting for a cabinet set. the pins are splintering a bit at the very tips when i try to pare them down to size. i've checked my chisels and they feel sharp, but i keep getting these tiny little crushed fibers instead of a clean cut. any idea what i might be doing wrong with my grain management or tool angle?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This splintering often happens when the wedge forces you are putting on the chisel are too aggressive for the end grain. Try alternating your cuts; instead of just pushing down, use a gentle rocking motion to shave thin layers off the tips. Ensure your chisel bevel is slightly more acute than you think it needs to be for end grain work to encourage shearing rather than crushing.",
      "source": "target",
