      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When the grain is complex, minimizing the downward pressure on the tip is crucial; try leaning your chisel slightly towards the grain direction while pushing. If you have areas with very inconsistent grain, consider using a specialized marking gauge or even a very sharp, thin knife alongside your chisel to carefully remove the bulk before fine-tuning. This allows you to manage the delicate fibers without heavy chiseling in those difficult spots.",
