    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, i'll try the knife method next time. one other thing though—it's almost like the wood is reacting unpredictably, like it's working against me. just when i think i've got the grain figured out, it'll snap or splinter in a way that feels... i don't know, intentional? like it's being stubborn for no reason. is that just a common thing with walnut when it's old or something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
