      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Walnut can be notoriously tricky due to its density and the varying tightness of its grain structure. Sometimes, what feels intentional is just the wood being at its natural limit against the forces applied. If you suspect a section is significantly harder or drier than the rest, proceed with extreme patience, using very light passes and allowing the tool to do the work rather than forcing it.",
